      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 1. Annual Financial Reporting of Net Worth and Income Required.\n(i) The Mayor, deputy mayors, agency heads, deputy agency heads, (ii) city employees in mayoral agencies who serve in the exempt or noncompetitive classes of civil service or who are provisional appointees, if the duties of such employees directly involve the negotiation, authorization or approval of contracts, leases, franchises, revocable consents, concessions and applications for zoning changes, variances and special permits, and (iii) any other city employees in mayoral agencies who serve in the exempt or noncompetitive classes of civil service or who are provisional appointees, who are requested by the Department of Investigation to comply with the provisions of this Order, shall annually file with the Department of Investigation a report on such form as shall be provided, setting forth the information required by section two of this Order. This annual report shall be filed for the calendar year and shall be submitted to the Department of Investigation no later than May 1 of the following year. For calendar",
